From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: drm/sun4i: de33: Send the flip event after the latch flush, never
 write the latch in active video

Three holes in the DE33 vblank register latch:

- The page-flip event was armed with drm_crtc_arm_vblank_event() and so
  sent by drm_crtc_handle_vblank(), before the vblank_quirk that writes
  the registers out. A client woken by it could commit the next frame
  before this one was in the hardware, and a flush that had to wait for
  a later vblank would still have reported the flip. The mixer now takes
  the event (new sunxi_engine_ops.hold_event) and sends it right after
  the flush that writes its commit, with that vblank's count and time.
  A new drain op writes out and sends what is left when the CRTC goes
  off. sun4i_crtc_atomic_begin() moves the event to scrtc->event for
  sun4i_tcon_finish_page_flip(), which also runs before the
  vblank_quirk: it leaves the event in the state for an engine that
  holds events, so every flip event (atomic, legacy page_flip and the
  helper's internal one) reaches atomic_flush.

- The snapshot (process context) took the planes and the blender shadow
  one after the other outside the latch lock, the flush (vblank IRQ) the
  other way round: an unsynced commit (legacy cursor) racing a flush
  could write one commit's planes with the next one's blender. Take both
  snapshots under the latch lock.

- de33_latch_flushes_late (0-1 per run in the writeback jobs, line
  339-369 of 806): the TCON vblank status bits are set at every vblank
  whether the interrupt is enabled or not, and only the handler clears
  them. drm_crtc_vblank_get() after the vblank interrupt had been off
  (vblank off delay, modeset) enabled it with a stale bit set, so the
  handler ran at once, mid-frame, and flushed the latch into active
  video. sun4i_tcon_enable_vblank() now clears the status bits in the
  enabling write (counted in sun4i_tcon vblank_stale_cleared).
  Independently of the cause, a vblank interrupt serviced too late for
  the flush to end inside the blanking (TCON line >= line_deadline,
  line_active minus ~50 us) now leaves the snapshot and its events for
  the next vblank (de33_latch_deferred), at most twice; then it is
  written anyway (de33_latch_forced) and late ones are not postponed
  until a flush lands in time again, so a mode whose line counter does
  not behave as assumed degrades to the old immediate write.

New read-only counters de33_latch_{line_deadline,deferred,forced,
events,events_now}. DE2/DE3, the A523 RCQ path and the TV encoder
mixer's register values are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
